-- Migration 0106: Batch 5 — CORE, CALF/LOWER LEG, KETTLEBELL
--
-- Roadmap X-37. The three groups from the Strava gap analysis that were genuine
-- capability gaps rather than naming granularity.
--
-- CORE (12). 54 exercises listed core as a primary muscle, but most were compounds
-- (goblet squat, push-up, pull-up). Dedicated core work was ~20 and almost entirely
-- anti-extension: plank variants. Missing outright were anti-rotation (no Pallof
-- press existed), loaded anti-lateral-flexion, and lower-ab flexion. Core drives a
-- whole progression axis, so the axis was being trained by one pattern.
--
-- CALF / LOWER LEG (8). Only 5 true calf-loading exercises, all straight-knee
-- (gastrocnemius). Absent: soleus work (bent knee), eccentric loading, and the
-- tibialis anterior. Those three are the ones that matter for running injuries,
-- and this app has two running coaches.
--
-- KETTLEBELL (10). A selectable equipment option with 6 exercises.
--
-- Every row carries loads_* injury tags (R563). Skill-heavy kettlebell lifts carry
-- explicit "learn it light first" cues.

INSERT INTO exercises
